/-
# Sheffer Algebra: The Algebraic Structure Generated by Softplus

The Sheffer algebra is the smallest set of functions ℝ → ℝ that:
1. Contains the softplus function σ(x) = log(1 + eˣ)
2. Is closed under affine pre-composition: if f is in the algebra, so is x ↦ f(ax + b)
3. Is closed under affine combination: if f, g are in the algebra, so is αf + βg + γ
4. Is closed under composition

This file formalizes the Sheffer algebra and proves key closure properties.
-/

